{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"aa870cd0534b1d1fb899c72be85669782d6e44e36f36b5c13ea39966317e95db","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar_reconciler integration test","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py:311","binding_store_mod._now_iso","binding_lifecycle._now_iso","clear_absent","binding_lifecycle.py:296","test_clear_absent_does_not_dirty_an_entry_with_no_absence"],"problem_keywords":["idempotency","oracle","clock patching","binding lifecycle","test coverage","integration test"],"propositions":["The idempotency oracle patches _now_iso only on binding_store, but clear_absent and siblings moved to binding_lifecycle during RP-02 S2 T2, causing the clock patch to no longer reach those operations.","The integration test still passes because the no-churn contract ensures the clock is never consulted on a healthy pass, but blast radius narrowed silently.","Patching _now_iso on both binding_store and binding_lifecycle restores the oracle's ability to catch regressions where moved operations unconditionally stamp updated_at.","The no-stamp contract for clear_absent is pinned at unit tier in test_binding_lifecycle.py, containing risk from the coverage movement."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787301662612866001,"uuid":"887162c3-d507-4050-afe8-ec0c8c926f42"}